Subject: [PATCH v2 00/16] Move beastie and lab-claude onto lab-mail
To: lab@lists.p7x.dev
Cc: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:33:25 +0000

This moves the list's two clients off the jj maildir and onto
lab-mail: beastie, for Pat, and lab-claude, for the agent. It is the
work planned in "Configure notmuch to use lab-mail" [1], and it
follows the client design approved in "[PATCH v2]
jails/instances/lab-mail: Spec the list's mail hub" [2]. The spec
text is in jails/instances/lab-mail/spec.org, in the same commits as
the code.

The setup is now in layers, and each host's config is its own:

- Ports. mail/isync, mail/msmtp, and mail/notmuch, from each host's
  ports list.
- Shared config. The notmuch package in dotfiles/notmuch ships the
  lab-mail profile's hooks, and samples of the profile's config,
  ~/.mbsyncrc, and ~/.msmtprc, with you@p7x.dev for the login. It
  installs no config of its own.
- Host config. beastie's lives in infra/hosts/beastie/mail, with
  your values, and "just install-mail" installs it. lab-claude's is
  in its jail's dist, as before. infra/hosts/beastie/README.org
  documents beastie's setup, from the ports to the password.

The patches come in phases, so you can stop after any of them:

- Support, patches 1-5. Nothing changes until a client uses it.
  beastie gets isync and msmtp. The notmuch package adds the lab-mail
  profile beside the default one, with the samples. lab-claude pulls
  all four folders into the profile, and can post with git
  send-email.
- Check and beastie, patches 6-8. "just check" in dotfiles/notmuch
  checks any host's client: it logs in to lab-mail, makes a dry run
  of the sync, checks the profile, and talks to msmtp without
  posting. Patch 7 adds beastie's configs. Patch 8 adds "just
  check-mail" in infra/hosts/beastie, which checks what is beastie's
  own and then runs the client check.
- Switch, patches 9-10. Emacs reads the profile and posts through
  msmtp, with an Fcc into sent. M i, M n, M l, and M a move the
  message or thread at point to INBOX, Next, Later, or Archive.
  lab-process-mail syncs before each pass and answers only approved
  senders.
- Cleanup, patches 11-16. The jj maildir pieces go, maildir-deliver.sh
  among them, deleted in patch 15.

Trying it on beastie before the switch, after patches 1-8, as Pat:

    cd ~/lab/default.jj/dotfiles/notmuch && just install
    cd ~/lab/default.jj/infra/hosts/beastie && just install-mail
    $EDITOR ~/.config/lab-mail/password
    mbsync lab-mail && NOTMUCH_PROFILE=lab-mail notmuch new
    just check-mail

The password goes in ~/.config/lab-mail/password, readable only by
you, and ~/.mbsyncrc reads it with PassCmd "cat ...". That keeps your
configs in the repo whole, with no secret in them. The other options
are Pass in ~/.mbsyncrc itself, a PassCmd that runs a password
manager, or neither, and mbsync asks on each run. The README lists
them. msmtp needs none, since lab-mail takes posts with no login.

The switch, in order:

1. Import the jj maildir as the README from v13 describes. That
   recipe files every old message in INBOX, so your inbox tag would
   then show every message from others that you have not answered.
   You may prefer to change the recipe's "Far :lab-mail:INBOX" to
   Archive.
2. Apply patches 9-10. Run just install in dotfiles/emacs on beastie,
   and in src/lab-process-mail on lab-claude.
3. Apply patches 11-16 whenever you like. After that, the mail
   bookmark on upstream and ~/lab/mail.jj on lab-claude can go.

Notes:

- The series is based on b/dev, but it needs nothing there except
  "[PATCH v13 0/8] jails/instances/lab-mail: Build the list's mail
  hub" [3].
- Tested: the notmuch package builds and installs into a scratch
  home. just install-mail installs each config, keeps a changed one
  as .old, and leaves the password file alone on a second run. With
  the package and beastie's configs installed in a scratch home here,
  and a wrong password, just check-mail fails only on the mbsync
  login and the dry run, which is what spec step 14 asks. Not tested:
  a run with your real password, which needs beastie.

Changes in v2:
- Your configs are explicit and live with beastie: patch 7 adds them
  in infra/hosts/beastie/mail, with just install-mail. The samples in
  dotfiles/notmuch use you@p7x.dev and Your Name, not your values,
  and the package no longer copies any of them into place. Patch 3
  now only adds the samples. (Pat, in [4])
- beastie has its own docs, infra/hosts/beastie/README.org, laid out
  as ports, then the shared package, then beastie's config. (Pat, in
  [4])
- No pass(1). The password is in a file only you can read, and the
  README gives the other options. pass came from lab-mail's spec and
  README, which said you keep the password in pass(1), and from
  sysutils/password-store in beastie's ports list. Patch 3 corrects
  both documents. (Pat, in [4])
- There is a check for beastie, patch 8, "just check-mail". The
  client check in patch 6 is for any host, and its spec step now runs
  on lab-claude only. (Pat, in [5])
- maildir-deliver.sh is deleted, not just no longer installed: patch
  11 drops the Emacs package's link to it, and patch 15 deletes the
  script, once nothing calls it. (Pat, in [6])
- The note in dotfiles/notmuch's README about trying the profile in
  Emacs beside the default one is gone, since patch 14 drops the
  default profile.
